      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Polar Coordinates in Log-Polar mode reads the picture's X as the angle around the middle and its Y as how far out, on a log scale. So the skewed checkerboard becomes a spiral, and sliding it up a little each frame zooms in forever. Try Mode Cartesian to Polar for plain rings, or turn the Stretch/Skew's Skew X."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
